<title>SPAIN: Spain's SEAT restarts production in Martorell.</title>
<headline>Spain's SEAT restarts production in Martorell.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen's Spanish unit Seat restarted car production at its Martorell plant on Wednesday, a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>He did not explain how the production, stopped since Friday night because of a two-week Spanish truckers strike, could be restarted. He just said they had used &quot;imaginative solutions&quot;.</p>
<p>Seat's Martorell plant cut its output by 4,000 cars because the strike hampered parts delivery.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
